    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-97885/blocks/prose-sec-004",
      "source": "sections/sec-004-11-mumps-disease.md",
      "source_hash": "ed610bd44ea942882bb427ce2bdfb3a5f5a8bc2275928f693fafb5bcc66e22e4",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Describes mumps as an acute viral illness marked by swelling of the parotid or other salivary glands, spread by contact with respiratory droplets or saliva and less infectious than measles or varicella. It explains how the virus replicates and spreads in the body and the timing of infectiousness. It lists complications such as orchitis, meningitis, encephalitis and deafness, with their frequencies.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-97885/blocks/prose-sec-005",
      "source": "sections/sec-005-12-mumps-virus.md",
      "source_hash": "fffc1f364f18332419e77ff156b51c7c4336cdcaa7c8572f79db23f01baabc30",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Describes the mumps virus as an enveloped, negative-sense RNA virus in the Paramyxoviridae family, with its size, genome and the proteins encoded by its genes. It notes the roles of the structural and nonstructural proteins and the genotyping scheme.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-97885/blocks/prose-sec-006",
      "source": "sections/sec-006-13-mumps-vaccines.md",
      "source_hash": "4cba7cd3a8828b9348c3e5f10861001957f19dd849804e0dfc5ea2881840ccc8",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Reviews mumps vaccines from the first inactivated vaccine of 1946, discontinued because immunity was short-lived, to the many live attenuated strains used since. It describes strains such as Jeryl Lynn, Urabe, Leningrad-3 and others, including how they were developed. A table compares reported rates of aseptic meningitis after vaccination with different strains in various countries.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-97885/blocks/prose-sec-007",
      "source": "sections/sec-007-2-immunological-response-to-natural-infection.md",
      "source_hash": "569c1c1786a3ee5ad7b1ccc8c47dbb3ef7f3a4b792b28303f5654d68240229e0",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Notes that immunity after natural mumps infection probably involves both antibodies and cellular immunity, that no definitive correlates of protection exist, and that research is limited compared with measles and rubella.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-97885/blocks/prose-sec-008",
      "source": "sections/sec-008-21-antibody-response-to-mumps-infection-in-unvac.md",
      "source_hash": "6b40791709dbf76a8fbf5e8dd550279821c79259f7e3b3c18cd883ba38d0ee4a",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Describes the antibody response to mumps in unvaccinated people, with IgM appearing within days of symptoms and peaking around one week. IgG rises to a peak in about three weeks and persists, while salivary IgA can be detected for several weeks.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-97885/blocks/prose-sec-009",
      "source": "sections/sec-009-22-cell-mediated-immunity-following-natural-mump.md",
      "source_hash": "b2fba495fff6c82a0f5ad7e4d5cf664cd5732772ab300593791c5a0a8ef906a3",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Describes cell-mediated immunity after natural mumps, noting that lymphocytes are thought to aid recovery but that little is known about mumps-specific cellular immunity. It cites studies linking cytotoxic and proliferative lymphocyte responses with infection.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-97885/blocks/prose-sec-010",
      "source": "sections/sec-010-23-maternal-antibody.md",
      "source_hash": "ae1eda1c04fc6fe913e0bdfc8dfdd5c720776d2e3bb776763ef3e2f3fb564d91",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Explains that maternal antibodies to mumps cross the placenta and likely protect infants, citing lower mumps rates in infants under one year. It reports studies on how long maternal antibodies remain detectable during the first year.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-97885/blocks/prose-sec-011",
      "source": "sections/sec-011-24-duration-of-immunity-to-natural-mumps-infecti.md",
      "source_hash": "a6869e6c04ed03faa514e54a49b217f4f7a812fdf555a5a5dcb6db5c493242d9",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Explains that natural mumps infection is generally thought to give long-lasting immunity, though confirmed reinfections have been reported and may be more common than believed.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-97885/blocks/prose-sec-013",
      "source": "sections/sec-013-31-antibody-response-following-vaccination.md",
      "source_hash": "a6a762278eca48b2d1b99e3dc599859a88910f4866528669d5afdae6c83bb184",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Reports that over 90% of children develop mumps antibodies after vaccination, with similar seroconversion across major vaccine strains, and discusses responses to one and two doses. A table summarizes seroconversion studies. It notes that revaccination raised antibody titres in more than half of recipients and reduced the share with low titres.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-97885/blocks/prose-sec-014",
      "source": "sections/sec-014-33-cell-mediated-immunity-following-mumps-vaccin.md",
      "source_hash": "a428280893f4e44496984729e4e5b29402b1841a0d21ecfa60b642b507277b2a",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Reports that most vaccinated children with mumps antibodies also show lymphocyte responses, that cellular responses are similar across ages regardless of maternal antibody, and that HLA associations suggest genetic influence on the immune response.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-97885/blocks/prose-sec-015",
      "source": "sections/sec-015-34-duration-of-immunity-to-mumps-vaccination.md",
      "source_hash": "187e362a8e0d8384edebc2b908feecf91ddaa281e2a881db2dda754133226cc7",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Notes that data on long-term immunity after mumps vaccination are limited, though antibodies persist in most people about ten years after one MMR dose, with variation by laboratory method. It discusses waning antibody levels after two doses. It ends by listing open questions on cellular immunity and boosting from exposure to wild virus.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-97885/blocks/prose-sec-016",
      "source": "sections/sec-016-35-correlates-of-immunity.md",
      "source_hash": "dc9aa39144babe911f5a3c7709a1d2bfda880cefd0388335740747b31a48c8e6",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Discusses correlates of immunity to mumps, explaining that neutralizing antibodies seem a reasonable marker though no serological test reliably predicts protection. It calls for more research, including on cell-mediated immunity markers.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-97885/blocks/prose-sec-017",
      "source": "sections/sec-017-4-laboratory-diagnosis-of-mumps.md",
      "source_hash": "e0dac0e89468d187d96a1b80c67468a42445e5d03af3c22fa4c3ac9c888018d9",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Notes that mumps is often diagnosed clinically from parotitis but that laboratory confirmation may be needed because other causes exist and mumps is becoming rare.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-97885/blocks/prose-sec-018",
      "source": "sections/sec-018-41-virological-methods.md",
      "source_hash": "df578371be6e1c0d9a19bcfbcbc27b2bc90b4deb557f9ad1e01e0c5bb13333d9",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Describes virological methods for diagnosing mumps, including virus stability in storage, specimen types and timing of collection. It notes that RNA detection by RT-PCR is generally more sensitive than culture.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-97885/blocks/prose-sec-019",
      "source": "sections/sec-019-42-serological-methods.md",
      "source_hash": "365c5c2d0442ca460fb1852e4cd240d93669f2ddcb578fcc2b64d8706153fbe9",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Describes serological diagnosis of mumps, explaining that IgM detection works well in unvaccinated patients if specimens are well timed but may fail in vaccinated people with a secondary immune response. A table sets out expected laboratory results by vaccination status and timing of collection.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-97885/blocks/prose-sec-020",
      "source": "sections/sec-020-43-diagnostic-challenges.md",
      "source_hash": "5e3ab84af53c0e9d24d95f535c9b4662394f2af486b3a9a6fffd8fbe41da8814",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Explains that laboratory diagnosis of mumps is difficult in highly vaccinated populations, as shown in the 2006 US outbreak, and that RT-PCR and culture are the best current tests for vaccinated people.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
